From 621d979f7b03f36cd2b0d4c1564cf5134745bfc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: what is not certain keeps only the output with
 the picture on, and a refused turn-off goes on one CRTC at a time

Monitors on the same card as the TV stayed on, black, with the picture on
the TV. Two paths in the code kept them on, and both are closed:

- Where it was not certain which output carries the sound in use (the audio
  engine had not said yet, ALSA names no card or no ELD, the ELD of the card
  reads as no display of it, which nothing says cannot happen with the ELD of
  an NVIDIA codec), every output of the card that could carry sound was kept
  on, monitors included. Only the output with the picture is kept now, as it
  is on anyway; the others go off. What was in doubt goes to kodi.log in one
  line per sound: why, the outputs that could have carried it with the
  display of each, and the display the ELD names. An exact match of the ELD
  still keeps that output, and hades-keep-outputs still keeps what the user
  names. This replaces the filter by EDID audio descriptors of the commit
  before, which would not have turned off a monitor with a headphone jack:
  the descriptors are still named in the log line.
- The commit that turns the unused outputs off was asked for three times
  and then given up ("they stay on"), so one CRTC that the driver refused
  kept every monitor lit. After the second refusal the outputs now go off
  one CRTC at a time; one that the driver refuses alone is left on and
  named, and the rest go off. A move to another output still turns them all
  off at once.

Not verified on hardware: that either was the cause on the 4080; the log
lines of its next test say which.
